.TH ORO-ZLIB 3 "" "Oro Runtime" "Oro Runtime API Manual"
.SH NAME
oro:zlib \- JavaScript API module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
import * as module from 'oro:zlib'
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Native zlib (v1.3.1) helpers exposed through the Oro runtime. This module provides convenient buffer\-based compression utilities as well as a streaming API built on top of the runtime's zlib service.
.PP
Examples:
.PP
import { deflate, inflate } from 'oro:zlib'
.PP
const compressed = await deflate(Buffer.from('hello')) const plain = await inflate(compressed)
.SH REFERENCE
.TP
\fBisAvailable()\fR
Reports whether the zlib primitive is available in the current runtime (based on native build configuration).
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<boolean>\fR
.TP
\fBdeflate(input, options)\fR
Compresses a buffer using zlib/deflate.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIinput\fR (Buffer \\| Uint8Array \\| ArrayBuffer \\| string; required)
.br
\fIoptions\fR (ZlibOptions; optional; default null)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<Buffer>\fR
.TP
\fBinflate(input, options)\fR
Decompresses a buffer using zlib/inflate.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIinput\fR (Buffer \\| Uint8Array \\| ArrayBuffer \\| string; required)
.br
\fIoptions\fR (ZlibOptions; optional; default null)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<Buffer>\fR
.TP
\fBgzip(input, options)\fR
Compresses a buffer using gzip framing.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIinput\fR (Buffer \\| Uint8Array \\| ArrayBuffer \\| string; required)
.br
\fIoptions\fR (ZlibOptions; optional; default null)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<Buffer>\fR
.TP
\fBgunzip(input, options)\fR
Decompresses a gzip buffer.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIinput\fR (Buffer \\| Uint8Array \\| ArrayBuffer \\| string; required)
.br
\fIoptions\fR (ZlibOptions; optional; default null)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<Buffer>\fR
.TP
\fBZlibStream\fR
Represents a stateful zlib stream backed by the native runtime.
.TP
\fBcreate(mode, options)\fR
Opens a new zlib stream.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fImode\fR (ZlibMode; optional; default 'deflate')
.br
\fIoptions\fR (ZlibStreamOptions; optional; default null)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<ZlibStream>\fR
.TP
\fBwrite(chunk, options)\fR
Writes a chunk into the stream and returns the processed output chunk.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIchunk\fR (Buffer \\| Uint8Array \\| ArrayBuffer \\| string; required)
.br
\fIoptions\fR (ZlibChunkOptions; optional; default null)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<Buffer>\fR
.TP
\fBend(chunk, options)\fR
Signals the end of the stream. An optional final chunk can be provided.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIchunk\fR (Buffer \\| Uint8Array \\| ArrayBuffer \\| string; optional; default null)
.br
\fIoptions\fR (ZlibChunkOptions; optional; default null)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<Buffer>\fR
.TP
\fBclose()\fR
Closes the stream without sending additional data. Subsequent writes will throw.
.TP
\fBcreateDeflateStream(options)\fR
Convenience helper for creating a deflate stream.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (ZlibStreamOptions; optional; default null)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<ZlibStream>\fR
.TP
\fBcreateInflateStream(options)\fR
Convenience helper for creating an inflate stream.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIoptions\fR (ZlibStreamOptions; optional; default null)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<ZlibStream>\fR
